The Notice of harvesting operations required by this division shall be provided for each separate tract upon which harvesting operations are to be conducted. Such notice shall be made in such form or format as prescribed by rule or regulation of the Director of the Georgia Forestry Commission, and shall include the following information:
(1) A map of the area which identifies the location of the tract(s) where harvesting operations will be conducted and, as to those trucks which will be traveling to and from such tract(s) for purposes of collecting and transporting loads of cut forest products, the main point of ingress to such tract(s) from a public road and, if different from the point of ingress, the main point of egress from such tract(s) to a public road. If multiple points of ingress and/or ingress will be used, all such points shall be identified;
(2) A statement as to whether the timber will be removed from the tract(s) identified in the notice pursuant to a lump sum sale, a per-unit sale, or as an owner harvest for determination of the appropriate method of ad valorem taxation pursuant to the provisions of O.C.G.A. § 48-5-7.5;
(3) The name, address, and daytime telephone number of the timber seller if the harvest is pursuant to a lump sum or per-unit sale, or of the timber owner if the harvest is an owner harvest; and
(4) The name, business address, business telephone number, and nighttime or emergency telephone number of the individual or entity conducting timber harvesting operations.
(Ord. of 6-20-23(1), § 2)

